&lt;p&gt;Thanks for your interest in Oklo! We are searching for an Instrumentation &amp;amp; Controls Technician to join our team in Idaho Falls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oklo is transforming the future of energy, and we are looking for an experienced Instrumentation &amp;amp; Controls Technician to support the design, fabrication, commissioning, and operation of test platforms used in advanced nuclear technology development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate has broad, hands-on instrumentation experience and strong familiarity with the Emerson DeltaV distributed control system. Experience working under a nuclear quality assurance program, particularly ASME NQA-1, is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific responsibilities may include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instrumentation Installation and Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Install, terminate, configure, and verify sensors, transmitters, control valves, analyzers, data-acquisition equipment, and associated electrical and pneumatic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Control System Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Configure, operate, troubleshoot, and maintain distributed control systems, programmable logic controllers, data-acquisition systems, human-machine interfaces, and test control hardware. Support development and modification of Emerson DeltaV configurations, graphics, alarms, and control strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Platform Fabrication:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the fabrication and assembly of test platforms, including instrument panels, control cabinets, junction boxes, cable trays, conduit, tubing, wiring, and pneumatic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Support test readiness reviews, equipment startup, test execution, shutdown, and post-test activities. Monitor instrumentation and control-system performance during testing and respond to abnormal or unexpected conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Troubleshooting and Maintenance:&lt;/strong&gt; Diagnose and correct instrumentation, electrical, communications, controls, and data-acquisition issues. Perform preventive maintenance and recommend improvements that increase reliability, maintainability, and test efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Procurement and Equipment Selection:&lt;/strong&gt; Assist with the selection and procurement of instrumentation, controls equipment, calibration tools, electrical components, and test-platform materials. Coordinate with suppliers and verify that procured equipment meets technical and quality requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate degree, technical diploma, apprenticeship, military technical training, or equivalent practical experience in instrumentation, controls, electronics, electrical technology, industrial automation, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years of hands-on experience with industrial instrumentation, control systems, test systems, process facilities, or similar equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience installing, calibrating, commissioning, maintaining, and troubleshooting industrial instrumentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret electrical schematics, wiring diagrams, loop diagrams, piping and instrumentation diagrams, instrument data sheets, and equipment manuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with common industrial signals and protocols, including 4–20 mA, discrete I/O, HART, and Ethernet-based communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using calibration and diagnostic equipment such as digital multimeters, process calibrators, pressure calibrators, loop simulators, communicators, and electrical test equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift, move, and position equipment weighing up to 30 pounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong familiarity with the Emerson DeltaV distributed control system, including system operation, hardware, I/O, configuration, graphics, alarms, control modules, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting thermal-hydraulic, mechanical, chemical, high-temperature, high-pressure, or liquid-metal test systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in nuclear, aerospace, defense, pharmaceutical, chemical processing, power generation, or another highly regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ASME NQA-1 requirements, particularly requirements related to test control, calibration, procurement, document control, and configuration management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instrumentation Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Broad knowledge of industrial measurement technologies, including temperature, pressure, flow, level, position, force, strain, vibration, and other process or test measurements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience with distributed control systems, programmable logic controllers, data-acquisition systems, control loops, alarm systems, and industrial communication networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable working in a fast-paced development environment where priorities, equipment configurations, and test requirements may evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;A startup person&lt;/span&gt;: You aren&#39;t driven by titles or hierarchy, and prefer efficiency to excess process. You don&#39;t need or expect to have a lot of guidance but you enjoy working in a fast-paced team. If you prefer the culture and feel of a large organization, that is great, but you likely won’t enjoy working with us! There is plenty of important work and plenty of good opportunities with organizations like that.&lt;/p&gt;
