&lt;p&gt;Thanks for your interest in Oklo! We are searching for a Materials Test Engineer to join our team in Idaho Falls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oklo is transforming the future of energy, and we are looking for a Materials Test Engineer to plan, develop, and execute materials-testing programs that support advanced nuclear technology development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will support materials and components throughout the test lifecycle—from defining test objectives and preparing specimens through laboratory execution, data analysis, failure investigation, and final reporting with travel up to 10%.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong materials-science fundamentals with practical test experience. You should be comfortable developing test methods, operating laboratory equipment, reviewing specimen preparation, assessing data quality, interpreting material behavior, and communicating technically defensible conclusions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific responsibilities may include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Program Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate engineering data requirements into executable tests. Prepare test plans, laboratory procedures, work instructions, equipment requirements, inspection points, and data-collection methods for materials-characterization activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead or support test setup, readiness reviews, equipment checkout, specimen installation, startup, monitoring, shutdown, and post-test activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Validation and Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Review raw data for completeness and validity, identify anomalies, assess measurement uncertainty, calculate material properties, evaluate repeatability, and compare results with expected behavior or established requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Procurement Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Assist with the selection and procurement of laboratory equipment, reference materials, specimens, consumables, fixtures, instrumentation, and testing services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare test reports, materials evaluations, failure-analysis reports, engineering memos, data summaries, and recommendations. Clearly document methods, assumptions, deviations, results, uncertainties, and conclusions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Laboratory Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Help establish and improve materials-laboratory capabilities, equipment-maintenance programs, calibration practices, specimen-storage methods, test templates, and safe operating procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in materials science and engineering, metallurgical engineering, mechanical engineering, welding engineering, nuclear engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience interpreting test data and preparing clear technical reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift, move, and position objects weighing up to 30 pounds, with or without reasonable accommodation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license and ability to operate motor vehicles when required for assigned work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in materials science, metallurgy, mechanical engineering, welding engineering, nuclear engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing materials for nuclear, aerospace, defense, power-generation, chemical-processing, or other highly regulated applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with molten sodium or other molten alkali-metal systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ASME NQA-1 requirements, particularly requirements related to test control, calibration, procurement, document control, material traceability, and configuration management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or commissioning laboratory equipment, fixtures, environmental chambers, or custom test systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Materials Engineering Fundamentals:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong understanding of physical metallurgy, mechanical behavior, microstructure, phase transformations, heat treatment, degradation mechanisms, and material-processing relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Ability:&lt;/strong&gt; Able to interpret complex data, distinguish material behavior from test artifacts, identify trends and anomalies, and develop technically defensible conclusions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Clearly communicates test requirements, material conditions, technical risks, results, uncertainties, and recommendations to multidisciplinary teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Works effectively in a research and development environment where test needs, equipment configurations, and technical priorities may evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
