&lt;p&gt;Thanks for your interest in Oklo!&amp;nbsp; We are searching for a Software Lifecycle Specialist&amp;nbsp;to join our team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be focused on strengthening our software development lifecycle, ensuring high-quality delivery, and maintaining compliance with internal and regulatory standards. We support a&amp;nbsp;variety of internal “customers” and establish the processes, tooling structures, and governance&amp;nbsp;frameworks that allow engineering teams to execute effectively and transparently. Oklo is a fast-&amp;nbsp;moving startup, and we are actively formalizing lifecycle rigor while preserving engineering&amp;nbsp;velocity. You will have the opportunity to shape how software is scoped, tracked, governed, and&amp;nbsp;released across the company. A nuclear background is not required, but strong systems thinking,&amp;nbsp;attention to detail, a proactive mindset, and a sense of curiosity about the domain are all essential&amp;nbsp;in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific responsibilities may include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Members of the Systems Enablement team help align tooling, governance, and execution across&amp;nbsp;engineering domains. In this role you might:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain software lifecycle standards, templates, and workflows across GitLab and Jira.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and enforce traceability between requirements, design artifacts, code, testing, and&amp;nbsp;validation activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineers to ensure proper scoping, backlog hygiene, and milestone alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define change control and configuration management expectations in collaboration with&amp;nbsp;DevOps/Engineering Infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit readiness by ensuring lifecycle documentation and records are complete and reproducible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define lifecycle standards including Definition of Done expectations and release controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reporting and dashboards that provide visibility into lifecycle health, risk, and delivery status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in the software lifecycle and improve engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate compliance requirements into practical, implementable engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and recommend tooling improvements that strengthen lifecycle integrity without introducing unnecessary process overhead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Weʼd like to see a clear track record of the following, based on your past roles and experience:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelorʼs degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or equivalent industry experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in software development, DevOps, technical program management, software quality, or systems engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in regulated or compliance-driven environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software development lifecycle concepts including requirements traceability, version control, CI/CD, configuration management, validation, and release control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Jira or similar issue tracking systems in a structured, milestone-driven environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience documenting processes clearly and unambiguously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in ambiguous environments and building structure where none exists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior experience with our stack and tools is helpful, but not required:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting NQA-1, ISO 9001, NIST, or similar regulatory or compliance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GitLab, especially GitLab CI/CD and repository governance controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining or auditing SDLC frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building dashboards or lifecycle reporting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting engineering organizations with hardware, simulation, or embedded&amp;nbsp;systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CAD or PLM lifecycle controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing or maintaining work instructions and formal procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with secure software development lifecycle frameworks such as CSSLP or similar certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;A startup person&lt;/span&gt;: You aren&#39;t driven by titles or hierarchy, and prefer efficiency to excess process. You don&#39;t need or expect to have a lot of guidance but you enjoy working in a fast-paced team. If you prefer the culture and feel of a large organization, that is great, but you likely won’t enjoy working with us! There is plenty of important work and plenty of good opportunities with organizations like that.&lt;/p&gt;
